[E0134] Error: a precision is a float's, and this is `i64`
   ╭─[ err/388_precision_and_radix_of_the_wrong_type/main.wip:7:16 ]
   │
 7 │     val a = "\(n, precision: 2)"
   │                   ────┬────
   │                       ╰────── not a float
   │
   │ Note: a precision is how many digits a float is written with after its point: `\(seconds, precision: 3)`
───╯
[E0134] Error: a radix is an integer's, and this is `f64`
   ╭─[ err/388_precision_and_radix_of_the_wrong_type/main.wip:8:16 ]
   │
 8 │     val b = "\(x, radix: 16)"
   │                   ──┬──
   │                     ╰──── not an integer
   │
   │ Note: a radix is the base an integer is written in: `\(byte, radix: 16)`
───╯
[E0134] Error: a radix is an integer's, and this is `String`
   ╭─[ err/388_precision_and_radix_of_the_wrong_type/main.wip:9:30 ]
   │
 9 │     val c = "\(String::of("t"), radix: 2)"
   │                                 ──┬──
   │                                   ╰──── not an integer
   │
   │ Note: a radix is the base an integer is written in: `\(byte, radix: 16)`
───╯
